  "prerequisites": [
    "Use ordinary dynamic CREATE TABLE processing, not CREATE SCHEMA schema-processor execution, so the two explicit parent enforcing indexes are created by this run.",
    "Source and replay require ALTER or REFERENCES on the parent table (or REFERENCES on both nominated parent-key columns), in addition to creation and storage privileges.",
    "After parent CREATE TABLE, create both enforcing indexes successfully before the child action. The child has no PRIMARY KEY or UNIQUE constraint requiring a post-action index.",
    "Extract and replay the whole dependency closure: both table spaces, both tables, and both parent enforcing indexes. Raw CHECK text is compared without rewriting; behavioral CHECK and referential probes remain a harness responsibility.",
    "Per-case cleanup drops the two dedicated table spaces, child first; they own their tables and indexes. Never issue DROP INDEX against an enforcing index, and never add unrelated objects to campaign spaces."
  ],
